olls/articleshow/135981165.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135981165.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/aaps-losing-ground-former-leader-navdeep-singh-sangha-joins-bjp-ahead-of-punjab-polls/articleshow/135981165.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/aaps-losing-ground-former-leader-navdeep-singh-sangha-joins-bjp-ahead-of-punjab-polls/articleshow/135981165.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T13:01:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ayush Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135981378,imgsize-110644.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[PM Modi pays tribute to former PM Indira Gandhi on birth anniversary]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pm-modi-pays-tribute-to-former-pm-indira-gandhi-on-birth-anniversary/articleshow/135979717.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135979717.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[On the occasion of Indira Gandhi's birth anniversary, Prime Minister Narendra Modi and Karnataka chief minister D K Shivakumar paid tribute to her legacy. PM Modi shared a heartfelt message on X, recognizing her immense contributions to India's progress. Shivakumar referred to her as the 'Iron Lady,' praising her pivotal roles in sectors such as agriculture and banking, and underscoring her enduring influence on the country’s political landscape.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pm-modi-pays-tribute-to-former-pm-indira-gandhi-on-birth-anniversary/articleshow/135979717.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pm-modi-pays-tribute-to-former-pm-indira-gandhi-on-birth-anniversary/articleshow/135979717.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T12:26:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135980863,imgsize-114799.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Use of natural resources boomerang-ing back to bite': India accuses Pakistan of self-aggrandisement]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/use-of-natural-resources-boomerang-ing-back-to-bite-india-accuses-pakistan-of-self-aggrandisement/articleshow/135980128.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135980128.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[India flagged Pakistan's military establishment of exploiting the country's natural resources for personal gain and fomenting conflict with neighbours at a UNSC meeting. India's UN envoy Parvathaneni Harish also hit back at Islamabad for raising the Indus Waters Treaty, citing army chief Asim Munir's display of minerals to foreign leaders and calling on Pakistan's military to prioritise public welfare over self-aggrandisement.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/use-of-natural-resources-boomerang-ing-back-to-bite-india-accuses-pakistan-of-self-aggrandisement/articleshow/135980128.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/use-of-natural-resources-boomerang-ing-back-to-bite-india-accuses-pakistan-of-self-aggrandisement/articleshow/135980128.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T12:17:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135980178,imgsize-1409631.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘50cr Indians defeated poverty’: PM Modi counters Rahul’s ‘economic disaster’ remark, cites World Bank figures]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/50cr-indians-defeated-poverty-pm-modi-counters-rahuls-economic-disaster-remark-cites-world-bank-figures/articleshow/135979742.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135979742.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/50cr-indians-defeated-poverty-pm-modi-counters-rahuls-economic-disaster-remark-cites-world-bank-figures/articleshow/135979742.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/50cr-indians-defeated-poverty-pm-modi-counters-rahuls-economic-disaster-remark-cites-world-bank-figures/articleshow/135979742.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T11:53:47+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Subhadra Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135980030,imgsize-53718.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Malaysia to not remain visa free for Indian visitors from Jan 1, 2027]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/malaysia-to-not-remain-visa-free-for-indian-visitors-from-jan-1-2027/articleshow/135979679.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135979679.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Malaysia will end the visa exemption policy for Indian tourists beginning on January 1, 2027. This decision comes after an increase in Indians misusing the visa-free entry for employment purposes. The High Commission of India in Kuala Lumpur has issued warnings regarding these violations of immigration rules. Indian nationals must obtain a valid visa prior to travelling to Malaysia from this date onward.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/malaysia-to-not-remain-visa-free-for-indian-visitors-from-jan-1-2027/articles